  "Name": "Netterfield1977-e-HL5H-staggered",
  "Source": "R. P. Netterfield, \"Practical thin-film polarizing beam-splitters,\" Optica Acta 24(1), 69-79 (1977). doi:10.1080/713819379 - Fig. 3 caption case (e); text pp. 74-76",
  "Notes": "Cemented-cube polarizing beam-splitter, 633 nm; 11 layers with thicknesses staggered symmetrically about the centre in a geometric progression (factor 1.3), ZnS:cryolite 1:2\nSpecification: Rp < 0.01 % and Ts < 0.1 % at 633 nm; Rp rises less sharply near the design wavelength\nReported: Theory: Rp < 0.01 %, Ts = 0.07 % at 633 nm (Rp does not reach exactly zero). Measured (Fig. 7): Ts = 0.09 %, Rp < 0.01 % at 633 nm.\nNotes: Symmetric stack so listing direction is immaterial. Odd layers are ZnS (H), even cryolite (L) per (HL)^5H. Values consistent with text: x = 199.8, x/1.3 = 153.7, x/1.3^2 = 118.2, x/(2*1.3^0.5) = 87.6. Design found iteratively; constant indices at 633 nm.\nLayers from Fig. 3 caption case (e); text pp. 74-76; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours Ts 0.069 %, Rp 2.1e-3 % at 633 nm; paper Ts 0.07 %, Rp ~0 (theory).",
